  "question": "A force of 50 N acts on a body of mass 10 kg. Find acceleration.",
  "gold_answer": "# Solved Numerical\n\n---\n\n## Dynamics Problem\n\n### Problem\nA net force of $50 \\text{ N}$ acts on a body of mass $10 \\text{ kg}$. Find its resulting acceleration.\n\n### Given\n* Force applied ($F$) = $50 \\text{ N}$\n* Mass of the body ($m$) = $10 \\text{ kg}$\n\n### Formula\n$$F = ma$$\n\nRearranging to solve for acceleration ($a$):\n$$a = \\frac{F}{m}$$\n\n### Substitution\n$$a = \\frac{50}{10}$$\n\n### Calculation\n$$a = 5 \\text{ m/s}^2$$\n\n### Final Answer\n**Acceleration ($a$) = $5 \\text{ m/s}^2$**\n\n### Interpretation\nThis indicates that the $50 \\text{ N}$ force causes the $10 \\text{ kg}$ mass to increase its velocity uniformly by $5 \\text{ meters per second}$ every single second in the direction of the applied force vector.",
  "candidate_response": "# Physics Module: Dynamics\n\n┌──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n│ **Introduction**                                                         │\n│                                                                          │\n│ This problem explores the relationship between force, mass, and the      │\n│ resulting motion of an object, governed by Newton's Second Law of        │\n│ Motion.                                                                  │\n└──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n\n┌──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n│ **Given Parameters**                                                     │\n│                                                                          │\n│ • **Force ($F$):** $50\\text{ N}$                                         │\n│ • **Mass ($m$):** $10\\text{ kg}$                                         │\n└──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n\n┌──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n│ **Main Formula: Newton's Second Law**                                    │\n│                                                                          │\n│                         $$a = \\frac{F}{m}$$                              │\n│                                                                          │\n│ **[ Explain Formula ]**                                                  │\n│ Acceleration ($a$) is directly proportional to the net force acting on   │\n│ an object and inversely proportional to its mass.                        │\n│                                                                          │\n│ **[ Open Formula Lab ]**                                                 │\n│ Variables:                                                               │\n│ - $F$ (Force in Newtons)                                        